# Cloudflare Pages edge + browser caching rules. Before this file the large
# /models/*.glb (~13 MB total) served with no Cache-Control - Cloudflare reported
# cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC (revalidated every visit, never edge-cached), the
# single biggest cheap repeat-visit cost. These rules cache the heavy, stable
# static assets hard so a returning visitor re-downloads nothing.
#
# NB: Cache-Control governs the BROWSER cache. Cloudflare's EDGE only caches
# extensions on its default list - .glb/.json are not on it, so the edge needs
# a Cache Rule in the Cloudflare dashboard (Rules -> Cache Rules: hostname
# courtgranville.com AND URI path starts with /models/ OR equals
# /nucleus-paths.json -> Eligible for cache). Verified 2026-06-05: without it
# the models report cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC on every request.

# Fingerprinted Astro build output - the filename changes whenever the content
# does, so it is safe to cache forever and skip revalidation entirely.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Textured 3D models (~1-3 MB each, the bulk of the page weight). Paths are not
# fingerprinted, so this is a long TTL but NOT immutable: a re-exported model is
# still picked up on an explicit reload, and a deploy purges the edge copy.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# Optimised project imagery and other static media (unhashed, content-stable).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# Nucleus contour paths - fetched at runtime by the hero + the atom island, stable.
/nucleus-paths.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# Stable documents + the social card (the 3.4 MB booklet PDF especially).
/*.pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/og.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# ── Security headers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CSP ships REPORT-ONLY first (nothing breaks; violations log to the console)
# and is flipped to enforcing only after a clean walk of every page + the booklet
# + a form submit on a preview deploy. The directive set is the pragmatic one for
# this stack, each relaxation deliberate:
#   - script-src 'unsafe-inline': the is:inline theme script (must be inline for
#     no-flash), the import map and the hero's inline module cannot be nonced in
#     a static Astro build. Low XSS surface: static site, no user content.
#   - style-src 'unsafe-inline': Astro scoped styles + inline style attributes.
#   - cdn.jsdelivr.net: three/lenis via the import map + pdf.js (script, its
#     worker, and connect for the dynamic import).
#   - static.cloudflareinsights.com / cloudflareinsights.com: Cloudflare Web
#     Analytics, injected by Cloudflare itself (verified in the network log).
#   - api.web3forms.com: the contact form (fetch + the no-JS form-action path).
#   - No SRI / import-map integrity: a considered position - support is uneven
#     and a hash mismatch silently kills the hero; version-pinned immutable CDN
#     URLs + this origin allow-list are the supply-chain control.
# HSTS starts deliberately SHORT (300s) - raised to a year only after the headers
# prove clean in production; never add `preload` without an explicit decision.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=300
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://api.web3forms.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
